# Example environment file for Mylonite.
#
# Mylonite ships with NO default LLM provider. You must configure one before
# any command that calls an LLM (Phase 1+: `scan`, `generate`, `validate`).
# All LLM calls go through LiteLLM, so any LiteLLM-supported provider works.
#
# Anthropic and OpenAI are both first-class targets. You can keep keys for
# more than one provider in this file; `MYLONITE_LLM__PROVIDER` decides
# which is *used* for a given run, so swapping is a one-variable change.
# Do not commit your real .env file — see .gitignore.

# Pick the active provider + model (required before any LLM call).
# MYLONITE_LLM__PROVIDER=anthropic
# MYLONITE_LLM__MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6
# MYLONITE_LLM__PROVIDER=openai
# MYLONITE_LLM__MODEL=gpt-4o

# Anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Azure OpenAI
# AZURE_API_KEY=
# AZURE_API_BASE=
# AZURE_API_VERSION=

# AWS Bedrock (uses standard AWS credentials chain)
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_REGION_NAME=

# Local model server (e.g. Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio)
# OPENAI_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=not-needed
